2026-10-28T17:22:54.8544117Z {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QzNt7Bi7guDJ8E4cqXpXmg","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"issue\": {\n    \"number\": 15,\n    \"title\": \"aws_athena_capacity_reservation target_dpus validation minimum should be 4, not 24\",\n    \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n    \"labels_at_open\": [\n      \"bug\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"as_of\": \"2026-06-10T15:49:38+00:00\",\n  \"form\": {\n    \"template\": \"Report a Bug\",\n    \"missing_required\": [],\n    \"empty_optional\": [],\n    \"used_form\": true\n  },\n  \"services\": {\n    \"resources_mentioned\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"aws_athena_capacity_reservation\",\n        \"resource_exists\": true,\n        \"data_source_exists\": false,\n        \"service_label\": \"service/athena\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"regex_labeler_would_apply\": [\n      \"service/athena\"\n    ],\n    \"primary_service_label\": \"service/athena\"\n  },\n  \"versions\": {\n    \"terraform\": \"1.5.7\",\n    \"provider\": \"6.49.0\",\n    \"latest_release\": \"6.49.0\",\n    \"latest_release_date\": \"2026-06-04\",\n    \"provider_status\": \"current\",\n    \"minor_releases_behind\": 0,\n    \"newer_release_notes\": [],\n    \"newer_fixes\": []\n  },\n  \"similar_issues\": [\n    {\n      \"number\": 34769,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#34769\",\n      \"title\": \"[Enhancement]: Support for Athena Capacity Reservations\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Adds support to be able to manage Athena Capacity Reservations * aws_athena_capacity_reservation terraform resource \\\"aws_athena_capacity_reservation\\\" \\\"example\\\" { name = \\\"example\\\" target_dpus = 5 tags = { project = \\\"terraform\\\" } } - - - - - None\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2023-12-06T18:08:02Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.563,\n      \"band\": \"likely\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 44349,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#44349\",\n      \"title\": \"[Ehancement]: Support for Athena Capacity Reservations Workgroup Assignments\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"When creating a Athena Capacity Reservation, we would like to be able to specify which workgroups can use it. Currently we will have to attach the workgroups after terraform application manually (e.g making a null_resource and running an AWS CLI command to update the assignments). * aws_athena_capacity_reservation hcl resource \\\"aws_athena_capacity_reservation\\\" \\\"example\\\" { name = \\\"example\\\" target_d\",\n      \"state\": \"open\",\n      \"state_reason\": null,\n      \"created_at\": \"2025-09-18T17:02:24Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.377,\n      \"band\": \"possible\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 46423,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#46423\",\n      \"title\": \"aws_subnet: ipv6_netmask_length validation rejects /64, reuses VPC-level constants\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"* aws_subnet The ipv6_netmask_length attribute on aws_subnet should accept the value 64, as documented (\\\"Valid values are from 44 to 64 in increments of 4\\\") and as required by AWS (IPv6 subnets are always /64). Terraform rejects ipv6_netmask_length = 64 during validation with: Error: expected ipv6_netmask_length to be one of [44 48 52 56 60], got 64 The value /64 is missing from the allowed set be\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-11T13:42:02Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.137,\n      \"band\": \"weak\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 44904,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#44904\",\n      \"title\": \"aws_bedrockagentcore_memory: Incorrect validation of `eventExpiryDuration`\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"* aws_bedrockagentcore_memory event_expiry_duration can be set between 1 and 365. Validated with numbers between 7 and 365. console $ terraform plan \\u2577 \\u2502 Error: Invalid Attribute Value \\u2502 \\u2502 with aws_bedrockagentcore_memory.example, \\u2502 on agentcore_memory.tf line 5, in resource \\\"aws_bedrockagentcore_memory\\\" \\\"example\\\": \\u2502 5: event_expiry_duration = 1 \\u2502 \\u2502 Attribute event_expiry_duration value must be bet\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2025-11-03T08:30:15Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.133,\n      \"band\": \"weak\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 40473,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#40473\",\n      \"title\": \"[Bug]: Apply fails with `error InvalidParameterValue: Serverless v2 maximum capacity 0.0 isn't valid. The maximum capacity must be at least 1.0.` when capacity is not specified\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"1.0.8 5.80.0 * aws_rds_cluster The apply should succeed even if config for ServerlessV2ScalingConfiguration is not specified. The apply failed with an error saying that a serverless maximum capacity 0.0 isn't valid. However, we did not specify a serverless capacity. It appears an empty/null value is being converted into 0.0. shell \\u2502 Error: updating RDS Cluster (x): operation error RDS: ModifyDBClu\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2024-12-06T00:08:16Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.132,\n      \"band\": \"weak\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"corpus_size\": 11153,\n  \"thresholds\": {\n    \"likely\": 0.4,\n    \"possible\": 0.28\n  }\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f5565a64-d076-4057-907b-a9a0d96fe91a","uuid":"d493985b-8544-411b-8cce-613f9c4b1f8b","timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:22:54.845Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"issue\": {\n    \"number\": 15,\n    \"title\": \"aws_athena_capacity_reservation target_dpus validation minimum should be 4, not 24\",\n    \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n    \"labels_at_open\": [\n      \"bug\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"as_of\": \"2026-06-10T15:49:38+00:00\",\n  \"form\": {\n    \"template\": \"Report a Bug\",\n 